# Append-only ledgers. Two branches each appending one row is not a conflict, it is two rows,
# and git cannot know that without being told. crew learned this on 2026-09-08 when two pull
# requests each appended one guard row and the second could not merge; this file exists so idp
# never spends a session on the same nothing.

# Keyed catalogs. Every shipping lane appends one class and one metric, so two lanes that never
# touched each other's work conflicted on the same last lines (idp#8615). bin/catalog-merge merges
# them by identity; the same key changed differently on both sides is still a conflict.
catalog/issue-classes.json merge=estate-catalog
catalog/optimus-metrics.json merge=estate-catalog
